# CODEOWNERS for pay-theory/payment-components
# GitHub uses the LAST matching line for each file. Every team listed on that line
# is asked to review, and an approval from any one of them satisfies the file.
# PCI DSS 6.2.3 / 6.5.1: non-author review on every change, plus the specialist
# team for infrastructure, dependency and card-data code.
# Each team needs write access to this repo, or GitHub ignores its lines.

# Default: any engineer other than the author
*                                 @pay-theory/developers

# Infrastructure, deploy scripts and CI
/shell/                           @pay-theory/infra-reviewers
/.github/                         @pay-theory/infra-reviewers

# Dependencies (any directory)
requirements*.txt                 @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
Pipfile                           @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
Pipfile.lock                      @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
pyproject.toml                    @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
poetry.lock                       @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
package.json                      @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
package-lock.json                 @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
yarn.lock                         @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
go.mod                            @pay-theory/dep-reviewers
go.sum                            @pay-theory/dep-reviewers

# Code that handles card data, keys, tokens or authentication
/src/                             @pay-theory/security-reviewers

# Changes to these review rules need a release approver
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @pay-theory/release-approvers
